☸️ Kubernetes Services

Spent some time understanding Kubernetes Services and why they are needed even when we already have Deployments managing our Pods.

One of the main things I understood is that Pod IPs are not permanent — when Pods are recreated, their IP addresses can change. A Service provides a stable way to access a group of Pods and keeps communication working even when Pods change.

Key concepts covered:

🔹 Why we need Services with Deployments
🔹 How changing Pod IPs create a need for a stable endpoint
🔹 Labels & Selectors and how they help identify and connect Pods with Services
🔹 Service discovery and how applications find other services inside a cluster
🔹 Different Service types:
   ClusterIP
   NodePort
   LoadBalancer
   ExternalName
🔹 How Services provide load balancing across Pods
🔹 How Services provide service discovery
🔹 How applications can be exposed internally or externally
🔹 Understanding the Service YAML configuration and its important fields

The most interesting part was understanding how Deployment manages the Pods, while Service provides a stable way to reach those Pods.

Another step forward in understanding Kubernetes networking and how different components communicate with each other. 🚀☸️

